<!-- ═══ FAQ ═══ -->
<section class="faq" id="faq">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p class="section-subtitle">Find answers to common questions about WorkerFinder</p>
        <div class="faq-container">
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question"><span>How do I create an account on WorkerFinder?</span><span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>Creating an account is simple and free. Click on the "Signup" button in the navigation bar, fill in your basic information including name, email, and phone number. You can register as a client or as a worker. Verify your email address to activate your account.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question"><span>How are workers verified on the platform?</span><span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>All workers on WorkerFinder go through a verification process including ID verification using CNIC, skill assessment, and background checks. Verified workers display a verified badge on their profile.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question"><span>What payment methods are accepted?</span><span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>WorkerFinder supports multiple payment methods including bank transfer, JazzCash, EasyPaisa, or cash on completion. All online payments are processed through secure payment gateways.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question"><span>Can I cancel a job after posting it?</span><span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes, you can cancel a job posting at any time before hiring a worker. If you have already hired a worker and need to cancel, please communicate with the worker through our messaging system.</p></div>
            </div>
            <div class="faq-item">
                <div class="faq-question"><span>What if I am not satisfied with the work?</span><span class="faq-icon">+</span></div>
                <div class="faq-answer"><p>Customer satisfaction is our priority. If you are not satisfied, first try to resolve the issue directly with the worker. If that does not work, you can file a complaint through our support system.</p></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

